  "final_message": "I've put `channel` back everywhere I removed it, but I couldn't run the tests or the arch check. Bash was denied for those commands, and I can't get approval in this session. I haven't confirmed that CI passes.\n\n`analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (enum `web|store|marketplace`). So the field wasn't unused, and I shouldn't have removed it.\n\nThe edits restore `channel` in these places:\n- **`src/core/order.ts`:** `CHANNELS`, `Channel`, the field on `Order` and `NewOrder`, the assignment in `createOrder`, and the validation.\n- **`src/core/events.ts`:** the field on `OrderPlaced` and its assignment in `orderPlaced()`.\n- **`src/api/requestParsing.ts`:** `POST /orders` reads and passes on `channel` again.\n- **Tests, `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`:** these match the state before my change. That includes the \"reports every problem at once\" test, which expects the `channel` error again.\n\nMy earlier change had already been committed as `38243ae` (\"gen\"), and I didn't make that commit. The restore is uncommitted on top of it. You can either commit it as is or revert `38243ae`.\n\nPlease run `npm test` and `npm run arch`, or re-run CI, to confirm.",
